# Site-specific patterns for the pre-commit hook.
#
# Copy to the path `git rev-parse --git-path secret-patterns` prints (inside
# .git/, so it is never committed) and list what this machine must not publish:
# an employer domain, an internal host, an issue-tracker prefix, a real name.
# Keeping them out of the repo is the point - a tracked blocklist would publish
# the strings it blocks.
#
# One POSIX extended regex per line, as awk reads them: no `\b` word boundary,
# and matching is case-sensitive - spell out both cases when it matters.
# Optional "<regex><TAB><label>" names the hit in the error message. Blank lines
# and # comments are ignored.
#
# Examples (commented out - they match nothing until you edit them):
#
# [Ee]xample-corp\.com	employer domain
# git\.example-corp\.com	internal git host
# (^|[^A-Za-z0-9])(AB|CD)-[0-9]{2,6}($|[^0-9])	issue id
# Jane Doe	real name
